  "body": "Tender: Closes on Wednesday 4 November 2026 at 2:00PM  (unless sold prior)\r\n\r\nFirst time offered in 60 years.\r\n\r\nPurchased by a ship's captain in 1966 for his family, this classic 1950's weatherboard home sits elevated overlooking the North Shore Cricket Pavilion with views to Rangitoto Island, North Head, and Mount Victoria, with a short flat stroll to Cheltenham Beach and King Edward Parade along the waterfront.\r\n\r\nSitting proudly on a flat 625m northwest-facing section, this is a unique opportunity to secure a home in a prized coastal pocket. Sun-drenched living and entertaining spaces are perfect for alfresco dining, family gatherings or relaxing afternoons in the sun.\r\n\r\nWith internal access to the three-car garaging, a storage room at the rear, and additional off-street parking for two more cars, this home boasts a rare find in this world-class seaside neighbourhood.\r\n\r\nThis home features three very large bedrooms and three bathrooms, possessing the charm and build of its era with the polished Matai flooring and the cedar and rimu windows. Move in and enjoy the beaches, local cafes, parks and top-tier schooling, with Devonport Village and CBD ferry connection close at hand.\r\n\r\nThese homes are always in great demand so call me today for an immediate viewing.",
